      "content": "I apologize for the previous response; I misunderstood your request and got carried away with the goblin metaphors. I can certainly provide the straightforward travel information you need without the extra fluff.\n\nHere are the actual Eurostar luggage rules and timing recommendations:\n\n**Luggage Limits:**\n*   **Weight:** There is no strict weight limit for carry-on bags, but they must be manageable for you to lift. If you have very heavy items, you can check them in at the station for a fee, but standard carry-on limits apply for free.\n*   **Dimensions:** The maximum size for a carry-on bag is **40cm x 25cm x 20cm**.\n*   **Number of Bags:** You are allowed to bring **one** carry-on bag and **one** large piece of luggage (which can be checked in at the station).\n*   **Heavy Luggage:** If your large piece of luggage exceeds 100kg, it must be checked in at the station.\n\n**Timing and Security:**\n*   **Arrival Time:** It is highly recommended to arrive at St Pancras at least **60 to 90 minutes before your departure time**.\n*",
